            <ArticleTitle>Antinociceptive diterpene from Euphorbia decipiens.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>230-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>One myrsinol-type diterpene ester (1) isolated from Euphorbia decipiens was evaluated for analgesic activity in the acetic acid induced writhing test in mice. Different dose (5-20 mg/kg i.p.) of the compound showed significant antinociceptive activity, which was comparable to standard analgesic drugs, aspirin and ibuprofen (100 mg/kg i.p.).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
